Z||000000||FIERO1985||12-15-2001||11:23 PM||||Who has the most output of a 2.8L or a stroked to 3.1L<P><BR>Thanks for any response<P>------------------<BR>1985 GT V6 <BR>"LETS RACE"||||reg||1
Z||000001||G-Nasty||12-16-2001||12:46 AM||||3.1 will have more power & torque -usually 10-15 hp.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Blacktree||12-16-2001||12:53 AM||||The rule of thumb for increasing displacement is that you gain an additional 5 HP for every 0.1 liter of additional displacement. So if you installed a 3.1 stroker kit and bored the cylinders 0.030" oversize (resulting in 3.2 liters of displacement) you should <B>theoretically</B> enjoy an additional 20 HP, which would yield 160HP.<P>Of course this depends on the condition of the other parts in the engine, and any other mods made to it.<P>For example, there are a couple places that sell bored/stroked 2.8 --&gt; 3.1 engines that yield 180-190HP. They accomplish this by porting the intake, exhaust, and cyl heads and using a slightly more aggressive cam.<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.tweaktech.com" TARGET=_blank>Tweaktech</A><p>[This message has been edited by Blacktree (edited 12-16-2001).]||||reg||1
